{
  "dom_id": "step-e3207",
  "name": "Example: Determining the Center of a Circle on the Coordinate Plane Using the Midpoint Formula",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13956659/assets/5015ee6cef1fdfa39002e2225e22fae050c38b4986410614e27f6e3cd5e1cdf6.png)\n\nFind the coordinates $(h,k)$ of the center of the circle above given that the points $(2,-3)$ and $(10,5)$ lie on a diameter of the circle.",
  "worked_solution": "The center of the circle is located at the midpoint of the diameter. Therefore, we can calculate it using the midpoint formula:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t(h,k) &= \\left( \\dfrac{x_1+x_2}{2}, \\dfrac {y_1+y_2}{2}\\right) \\[2pt]\n\t\t\t\t  &= \\left(\\dfrac{10+2}2,\\dfrac{5+(-3)}2\\right) \\[2pt]\n\t\t\t\t  &= \\left(\\dfrac{12}2,\\dfrac{2}2\\right) \\[2pt]\n\t\t\t\t  &= (6, 1).\n\t}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
